# vendor/xz: liblzma subset (raw LZMA2 encoder and decoder)

Kolmo's `ratio` mode (codec 6) codes blocks with raw LZMA2. Until rc3 the build linked the system liblzma
(`liblzma-dev` on Linux, Homebrew `xz` on macOS); it now builds this subset, so no build needs a system library and
every build runs the same liblzma.

## Provenance and verification

- Release: XZ Utils **5.8.1** (3 April 2025). Not 5.6.0 or 5.6.1 (the releases with the 2024 backdoor).
- Tarball: `https://github.com/tukaani-project/xz/releases/download/v5.8.1/xz-5.8.1.tar.gz`
  SHA-256 `507825b599356c10dca1cd720c9d0d0c9d5400b9de300af00e4d1ea150795543`.
- Signature: `xz-5.8.1.tar.gz.sig` from the same release page, verified with GnuPG on 16 November 2026:
  "Good signature from Lasse Collin <lasse.collin@tukaani.org>", RSA key
  `3690 C240 CE51 B467 0D30 AD1C 38EE 757D 6918 4620` (the key published at
  `https://tukaani.org/misc/lasse_collin_pubkey.txt`).
- Only C sources and headers are taken: no build scripts (autotools, CMake, m4), no test files, no assembly, no
  binary data. The 2024 backdoor lived in the build scripts and test files of 5.6.0/5.6.1; none of those kinds of file
  is here, and the build uses Kolmo's Makefile only.
- Every file below except the Kolmo files is byte-identical to the release (`cmp` against the verified tarball).

## What is kept

The public API needed by `lzma_raw_buffer_encode`, `lzma_raw_buffer_decode` and `lzma_lzma_preset`: the filter
chain plumbing (`common/filter_*`), the LZ encoder with all match finders and the LZ decoder (`lz/`), the LZMA1 and
LZMA2 coders (`lzma/`) and the range coder (`rangecoder/`). Four headers of the BCJ and delta filters are kept because
`filter_encoder.c` and `filter_decoder.c` include them unconditionally; none of their code is built. Not kept: the .xz
and .lzma containers, integrity checks (CRC32/CRC64/SHA-256 code), BCJ and delta filters, multithreading, the index,
the command-line tools.

## Kolmo files (written for Kolmo, not part of the release)

- `config.h`: replaces the configure-generated header; enables exactly the coders above, no threads, `NDEBUG`.
- `kolmo_crc32_table.c`: defines `lzma_crc32_table` from the release's generated table headers. The LZ match finders
  hash with its first row; upstream defines it in `check/crc32_fast.c` with code Kolmo does not need.
- `kolmo_lzma_namespace.h`: renames every external symbol to `kolmo_lzma_*` (forced include, see the Makefile), so
  `libkolmo.so` can share a process with the system liblzma (Python's `lzma` module loads it).
  Regenerate with `benchmark/rc3/deps/gen_lzma_namespace.sh`.
- `kolmo_lzma.h`: the header Kolmo includes instead of `<lzma.h>`.

## Output

LZMA2 output is byte-identical to the system liblzma 5.4.5 that built rc2's expected frames: the determinism check
(`benchmark/determinism/check.py`, 110 frames) passes unchanged, and raw LZMA2 at preset 9e of Silesia's xml, dickens
and x-ray is identical between the two libraries. Speed: see `benchmark/rc3/deps/RESULTS.md`.

## Updating

Download the new release and its `.sig`, verify the signature against the key above, copy the same file list from
`src/` of the release, rebuild, regenerate `kolmo_lzma_namespace.h`, and run the determinism check. Do not take any
release from 5.6.0 to 5.6.1.

